<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Despotate of the Morea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1349">1349</a>–<a href="/years/1460">1460</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Despotate of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> was a Byzantine province in the Peloponnese, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mystras">Mistras</a> by members of the imperial family with the title of despot. Growing from the fortresses ceded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> in 1262, it reconquered most of the peninsula from the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> by 1430, was a centre of late Byzantine learning, and fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1460.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/despotate-of-the-morea.jpg" alt="Despotate of the Morea" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas This file was derived from: Byzantine imperial flag, 14th century (firesteels vesion).svg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Byzantine_imperial_flag,_14th_century.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
